  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two identical glass rods <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> (refractive index = 1.5) have one convex end of radius of curvature 10 cm. They are placed with the curved surfaces at a distance d as shown in the figure, with their axes (shown by the dashed line) aligned. When a point source of light <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is placed inside rod <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> on its axis at a distance of 50 cm from the curved face, the light rays emanating from it are found to be parallel to the axis inside <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The distance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> is<br ><br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image13-905601a3-429c-47fb-9324-833fb2857ea6.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
